.TH S3M-RM 1 "" "s3m @VERSION@" "s3m Manual"
.SH NAME
s3m\-rm \- parallel object remover
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B s3m\-rm
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fBs3://\fIBUCKET\fR/\fIKEY\fR|\fIPREFIX\fR/|\fIMASK\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Removes objects in parallel using batched DeleteObjects requests.
By default this is a \fBdry run\fR: everything that would be removed is listed as CSV and nothing is deleted.
Add \fB\-\-apply\fR to delete.
.SS Target forms
.TP
.B s3://bucket/some/key
Exactly that key.
.TP
.B s3://bucket/some/prefix/
Everything under the prefix (note the trailing slash).
.TP
.B s3://bucket/logs/2024\-*
Glob mask (\fB*\fR, \fB?\fR, \fB[...]\fR; \fB*\fR also spans \fB/\fR).
Quote masks so the shell leaves them alone.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Actually remove.
.TP
.B \-\-permanent
On versioned buckets, delete every stored version and delete marker of the matched keys instead of just writing a delete marker.
Unrecoverable.
.TP
.B \-\-entire\-bucket
Allow a target that spans a whole bucket.
It is refused otherwise, and there is no short form.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-threads " N"
Worker threads, 1\-256 (default 16).
.TP
.BI \-\-shard\-depth " N"
Prefix levels expanded for parallelism, 0\-9 (default 2).
.TP
.B \-\-rrdns
Resolve the endpoint hostname to every A/AAAA address and spread worker threads across them, moving a thread to the next address if its current one fails.
See
.BR s3m (7).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " FILE"
Write the output to FILE and show a live progress display.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the console listing; progress and the summary are still shown.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH CONNECTION OPTIONS
The connection options \fB\-\-endpoint\fR, \fB\-\-region\fR, \fB\-\-profile\fR, \fB\-\-path\-style\fR, \fB\-\-no\-sign\fR, \fB\-\-insecure\fR and \fB\-\-ca\-bundle\fR are common to all s3m tools and are described in
.BR s3m (7).
.SH SAFETY
Overlapping targets are de-duplicated so no key is deleted twice.
A target spanning a whole bucket is refused unless \fB\-\-entire\-bucket\fR is given.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 completed with errors; 2 usage, startup or safety-guard refusal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR s3m (7)
.BR s3m\-ver (1),
.BR s3m\-find (1)
